WEBVTT

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.324
It is a contributor.

00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:02.368
Also, we know --

00:02:02.368 --> 00:02:04.412
we know what else ...

00:02:04.412 --> 00:02:05.413
email.

00:02:05.413 --> 00:02:07.290
A study a while back by McKinsey

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:12.253
showed that the average professional
spends 28 percent of their time

00:02:12.253 --> 00:02:13.796
just responding to email.

00:02:14.338 --> 00:02:16.007
Of course that drains us,

00:02:16.007 --> 00:02:18.426
of course that makes us busy.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.763
But the truth is, it’s also,
I believe, not the full picture.

00:02:23.181 --> 00:02:25.057
Those are manifestations.

00:02:25.057 --> 00:02:27.268
Those are problems, legitimately.

00:02:27.602 --> 00:02:32.148
But there are also some other things
going on underneath the surface,